########################################################################
#
# Based on DIME .gitignore template. Follow the instructions in the URL
# below to set up this template in your own repository
# https://github.com/worldbank/dime-github-trainings/tree/master/GitHub-resources/DIME-GitHub-Templates
#
# Note that if you are using GitKraken, you need to use version 5.x or more
# recent for this template to work properly
#
########################################################################

#######################
# Start by ignoring everything, and below we are explicitly saying
# what to not ignore
*

#######################
# List of files with GitHub functionality anywhere in the repo
# that we do not want to ignore

# These files include GitHub settings
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes

# Keep markdown files used for documentation on GitHub
!README.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!LICENSE*

#######################
# For performance reasons, if a folder is already ignored, then
# GitHub does not check the content for that folder for matches
# with additional rules. The line below includes folder in the
# top folder (but not their content), so that anything matching
# the rules below will still not be ignored.
!*/

#######################
# The following file types are code that should always be
# included no matter where in the repository folder they are
# located unless you explicitly ignore that folder

# Stata
!/**/*.do
!/**/*.ado

# R
!/**/*.R
!/**/*.Rmd
!/**/*.Rproj

# LaTeX
!/**/*.tex
!/**/*.bib

# Python
!/**/*.py
!/**/*.ipynb
# Still ignore .ipynb files in checkpoint folders
.ipynb_checkpoints
# Scratch notebook, not meant to be tracked
/test.ipynb

# Python / uv project config (needed to reproduce the environment)
!/**/*.toml
!uv.lock
!.python-version
# VS Code settings shared with the project
!.vscode/
!.vscode/*.json

# Matlab
!/**/*.m

# Markdown
!/**/*.md

# Julia
!/**/*.jl

#######################
# Include some additional file formats in any output folder. You might have
# to change the name of the Output folder to whatever it is called in your
# project, but we strongly recommend that you only include these files in
# a subset of the folders where you are certain no private data is ever stored.
!/**/Output/**/*.txt
!/**/Output/**/*.csv
!/**/Output/**/*.xml
!/**/Output/**/*.eps
!/**/Output/**/*.svg

#######################
# Include all the files with passwords or tokens here. All files named
# password or passwords are with this template ignored no matter which
# format you are using. Additionally, all content in any folder called
# password or passwords are also ignored. NOTE that your project might be
# using different names and then you must edit the lines below accordingly.
password.*
passwords.*
password/
passwords/

# Ignore all data files... (data/* en vez de data/ para poder re-incluir subcarpetas)
data/*
# ...salvo los YAML públicos de eval de idea 6 (Set A / pool del Set B, de Betley et al.)
!data/em-evals/
!data/em-evals/*.yaml

# ...y salvo el banco de casos ESCRITO PARA ESTE PROYECTO. No son datos de
# terceros con licencia: son parte del diseño experimental y sin ellos las
# corridas no se reproducen. Lo derivado (cases.jsonl, _meta.json) sigue
# ignorado porque lo regenera el script.
!data/research-desk/
!data/research-desk/cases_source.jsonl

# Lo que quedó fuera de uso al reencaminar el proyecto y nunca estuvo en git.
# Se conserva local (borrarlo lo perdía). Solo el README entra al repo, para que
# quede registro de qué hay ahí; los datos siguen sin commitearse — parte son de
# licencia restringida (ShareChat, CC BY-NC y gated).
!untracked-from-old-versions/
untracked-from-old-versions/**
!untracked-from-old-versions/README.md

# Lo que SI se versiona de results/. Desde el 2026-08-05 una corrida es una
# carpeta (results/<organismo>_<size>_<stamp>/), asi que hay que abrir la
# carpeta para llegar a los archivos: sin la regla de directorio, git no
# desciende y las excepciones de adentro no llegan a evaluarse nunca.
!/**/results/*/
# El reporte: es el resultado leible del experimento.
!/**/results/*/report.html
# El manifiesto del juez: registro de gasto real, que presupuesto.md cita como
# fuente del ledger. Chico y sin datos crudos.
!/**/results/*/manifest.json
# El acuerdo entre jueces (§5b).
!/**/results/*/agreement.md
# La config de la corrida: 1 KB que dice con que se genero cada resultado.
!/**/results/*/meta.json

# Los del esquema viejo, por si aparece alguno sin migrar.
!/**/results/*.html
!/**/results/step2_manifest_*.json
!/**/results/step2_agreement_*.md
